 Titmus was favored in this one."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Ledecky led the heats in 1:55.28 just ahead of Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/129511"} "Penny Oleksiak"] ", but Titmus was the fastest semi-finalist, finishing in 1:54.82, with Ledecky in third, also behind Hong Kong’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/130494"} "Siobhán Haughey"] ", with Oleksiak qualifying sixth for the final."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Oleksiak led the finalists through 50 metres in 26.50 when Haughey took over and led through 150 metres, with China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/2504727"} "Yang Junxuan"] " in second, Titmus in third, and Oleksiak fourth. Ledecky was never a factor and was never better than fifth place at any split, where she would finish."] "\n\n" [:p {} "As Yang faded on the last lap, Titmus came through with her typical fast finish, splitting 28.80 to win the gold medal in 1:53.50 for an Olympic record. Behind her, Haughey won Hong Kong’s first ever Olympic medal in swimming, a silver, and Oleksiak filled out the podium with a bronze, as Yang finished fourth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/140687"} "Ariarne Titmus"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "1:55.88 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "1:54.82 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:53.50 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/130494"} "Siobhán Haughey"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/HKG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/HKG.png"}] "HKG"]] [:td {} "1:56.48 (2 h3)"] [:td {} "1:55.16 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:53.92 (2)